@baseUrl=http://localhost:8000/api/v1/notifications
@notificationId=REPLACE_WITH_NOTIFICATION_ID
@adminToken=REPLACE_WITH_ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN
@selfToken=REPLACE_WITH_RETAILER_OR_SUPPLIER_ACCESS_TOKEN
@recipientId1=REPLACE_WITH_USER_ID_1
@recipientId2=REPLACE_WITH_USER_ID_2

# Notifications support multiple recipients; read/unread is tracked per
# recipient inside `recipients[]`, not as one shared flag on the document.
# DELIVERY_ASSIGNED notifications are also created automatically — see
# deliveries.http's POST (create delivery), which raises the business
# event this module listens for. See 00-smooth-flow.http for a chained
# run that ends with both a supplier and a retailer actually receiving
# one of these.

### create a notification (ADMIN only; sender_ref is always the caller)

POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
    "recipient_ref": ["{{recipientId1}}", "{{recipientId2}}"],
    "type": "DELIVERY_ASSIGNED",
    "title": "Heads up",
    "message": "Manual admin notice.",
    "actionUrl": "/pools/{{recipientId1}}"
}

### list my notifications (RETAILER/SUPPLIER — scoped to own recipient entry)

GET {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{selfToken}}

### list every notification (ADMIN — unscoped, full recipients[])

GET {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### get a notification by id (RETAILER/SUPPLIER must be a recipient; ADMIN sees any)

GET {{baseUrl}}/{{notificationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{selfToken}}

### mark my own notification read (RETAILER/SUPPLIER — only touches their
### own recipients[] entry; readAt is set automatically)

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/{{notificationId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{selfToken}}

{
    "isRead": true
}

### edit a notification's content (ADMIN only)

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/{{notificationId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
    "title": "Updated title",
    "priority": "HIGH"
}

### delete a notification (ADMIN only)

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{notificationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
